@page "/privacy-notice"
@model CDC.Web.Pages.PrivacyNoticeModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy notice";
}

<div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
        <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">Privacy notice for Disease Briefing, Decisions Support, Risk Assessment &amp; Ranking</h1>

        <p class="govuk-body">This notice explains how Disease Briefing, Decisions Support, Risk Assessment &amp; Ranking (D2R2) uses your personal information, and your rights over it.</p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Who we are and who controls your data</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">D2R2 is run by the Animal and Plant Health Agency (APHA), an executive agency of the Department for Environment, Food &amp; Rural Affairs (Defra).</p>
        <p class="govuk-body">Defra is the data controller for the personal information you give us through D2R2. A data controller decides how and why personal information is used.</p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">What personal information we collect</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">We collect:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>your name, email address and organisation</li>
            <li>your user name and the identifier your sign-in provider gives us, so we can recognise you when you sign in</li>
            <li>for APHA and Defra staff, your Defra account name and employee number, which we read from the Defra staff directory</li>
            <li>your role in D2R2 and the disease profiles you can work on</li>
            <li>the changes you make, such as contributions, review comments, notes and updates to reference and species data, with your name and the date</li>
            <li>records of when you sign in and use the service, kept in our security logs</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="govuk-body">We do not ask for, or collect, any special category information, such as information about your health or ethnicity.</p>
        <p class="govuk-body">We only use essential cookies. <a class="govuk-link" asp-page="/Cookies">Find out about the cookies we use</a>.</p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Why we collect it and our legal basis</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">We use your personal information to:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>let you sign in and give you access to the disease profiles and features your role allows</li>
            <li>record who contributed to and reviewed each disease profile</li>
            <li>send you emails about your access, such as how to sign in, and reminders when a profile you work on is due for review</li>
            <li>keep a record of changes, so we can check and correct the information in D2R2</li>
            <li>keep the service secure and find and fix problems</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="govuk-body">Our legal basis for using your personal information is that it is necessary to perform a task in the public interest, in the exercise of our official functions: monitoring and assessing the risk of animal diseases.</p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">What we do with it</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">When you sign in, we match you to your D2R2 user record and check what you are allowed to do. Your name is shown against the changes you make, and in the contributor and review lists of the profiles you work on.</p>
        <p class="govuk-body">We use your email address only to send you emails about D2R2.</p>
        <p class="govuk-body">We will not:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>sell or rent your data to third parties</li>
            <li>share your data with third parties for marketing purposes</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Who we share it with</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">We share your personal information with these suppliers, who process it for us under contract and only on our instructions:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>Amazon Web Services, who host D2R2 and its database</li>
            <li>GOV.UK One Login and Defra Customer Identity, who sign in external users</li>
            <li>Microsoft, who sign in APHA and Defra staff and provide the Defra staff directory</li>
            <li>GOV.UK Notify, who send emails for us</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="govuk-body">We may also share your information with other government departments and agencies when the law requires us to, for example to prevent fraud or other crime.</p>
        <p class="govuk-body">If you sign in with GOV.UK One Login, read the <a class="govuk-link" href="https://signin.account.gov.uk/privacy-notice">GOV.UK One Login privacy notice</a> to find out how it uses your information.</p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">How long we keep it</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">We keep your personal information only for as long as we need it for the purposes in this notice, or for as long as the law requires.</p>
        <p class="govuk-body">[To be confirmed by APHA: the retention period for user records, change records and security logs.]</p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Transfers outside the UK</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">[To be confirmed by APHA: whether any personal information is stored or processed outside the UK and, if so, how it is protected.]</p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Automated decisions</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">We do not use your personal information to make automated decisions about you.</p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">How we protect your data</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">We protect your data with encryption while it is sent and while it is stored, and only people who need it to run the service can see it. We make sure the suppliers who process it for us keep it secure.</p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Your rights</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">You have the right to ask for:</p>
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
            <li>information about how your personal information is used</li>
            <li>a copy of your personal information</li>
            <li>anything inaccurate in your personal information to be corrected</li>
            <li>your personal information to be erased when there is no longer a reason to keep it</li>
            <li>the use of your personal information to be restricted in some circumstances</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="govuk-body">You can also object to how your personal information is used.</p>
        <p class="govuk-body">Read the <a class="govuk-link" href="https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/animal-and-plant-health-agency/about/personal-information-charter">APHA personal information charter</a> to find out more about your rights and how to use them.</p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Contact and complaints</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">Contact the Defra Data Protection Officer if you have a question about this notice, want to use your rights, or think your personal information has been misused or mishandled.</p>
        <div class="govuk-inset-text">
            Data Protection Officer<br>
            Department for Environment, Food &amp; Rural Affairs<br>
            Seacole Building<br>
            2 Marsham Street<br>
            London<br>
            SW1P 4DF<br>
            <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:data.protection@defra.gov.uk">data.protection@defra.gov.uk</a>
        </div>
        <p class="govuk-body">You can also make a complaint to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO), the independent regulator for data protection.</p>
        <div class="govuk-inset-text">
            Information Commissioner's Office<br>
            Wycliffe House<br>
            Water Lane<br>
            Wilmslow<br>
            Cheshire<br>
            SK9 5AF<br>
            Telephone: 0303 123 1113<br>
            <a class="govuk-link" href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Make a complaint to the ICO</a>
        </div>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Changes to this notice</h2>
        <p class="govuk-body">We may change this privacy notice. When we do, the 'last updated' date below will change. If a change affects how we use your personal information, we will tell you.</p>
        <p class="govuk-body">Last updated: 23 November 2026</p>
    </div>
</div>
